    <section class="col">
      <p>
        <strong>When another tool fits better.</strong> HyperFrames has the larger feature set today (cloud
        rendering, a desktop app, voice and transcription tools, HDR and HLS output, a large block catalog) and a large
        community. Remotion suits teams that already work in React and want its mature ecosystem, if its license fits
        their company size. givemotion fits when you want no license conditions, no dependencies or telemetry, quick
        re-renders after many small edits, and checks that also look at pacing.
      </p>

      <!-- ============================================================ 6 -->
      <h2 id="limitations"><span class="n">6</span>Limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The evaluation is small.</strong> One or two runs per tool per brief, AI judges looking at frames rather than people watching, one machine. Read it as a running record.</li>
        <li><strong>No cloud rendering</strong>; it renders on your machine or server.</li>
        <li><strong>No visual editor</strong>; <code>givemotion dev</code> is a preview, and the agent is the editor.</li>
        <li><strong>No voice or transcription tools</strong>; bring a voice-over and a word-timed captions file or <code>.srt</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>No HDR or HLS output.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Slow on heavy pages without a GPU</strong>, and speed on a Mac is not benchmarked yet.</li>
        <li><strong>One open determinism case on macOS</strong> under heavy load; renders match on an idle machine.</li>
        <li><strong>It is young (0.x)</strong>; options may still change between minor versions.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- ============================================================ 7 -->
      <h2 id="start"><span class="n">7</span>Getting started</h2>
      <p>Requirements: Node.js 20 or newer and ffmpeg. Chrome is downloaded for you (<code>npx givemotion install</code>).</p>
      <pre><code>{`# a new project: a starter video plus the agent instructions
npx givemotion init my-video

# an existing project: only the agent instructions (Claude Code, Codex, AGENTS.md)
npx givemotion skill

# Claude Code plugin
/plugin marketplace add givemotion/givemotion
/plugin install givemotion@givemotion`}</code></pre>
      <p>Then ask your agent, for example: “Make a 20-second launch video for our app. Use our logo and colors, and put music under it.” Preview and scrub it with <code>npx givemotion dev my-video</code>.</p>

